1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,055
This is Tukang Copilot.

2
00:00:02,055 --> 00:00:06,508
Fix it yourself, safely, even in Javanese.

3
00:00:06,508 --> 00:00:09,685
“Aduh motorku mogok, bengkelnya tutup lagi.”

4
00:00:09,685 --> 00:00:15,116
In Indonesia, a small fault on a motorbike or a water pump can cost a day's wage.

5
00:00:15,116 --> 00:00:20,576
Repair videos can't see your problem, and most aren't in your language.

6
00:00:20,576 --> 00:00:23,208
Take a photo and say what's wrong.

7
00:00:23,208 --> 00:00:26,693
Every answer here is live from Meta's models.

8
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:30,180
The photos are AI-generated samples.

9
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:37,552
Each result shows up as soon as it's ready: what Muse Spark saw, the parts SAM outlined, then the likely cause.

10
00:00:37,552 --> 00:00:41,948
If it isn't sure, it asks one short question instead of guessing.

11
00:00:41,948 --> 00:00:43,248
Then the diagnosis.

12
00:00:43,248 --> 00:00:51,336
Likely causes with confidence, a safety level, tools and time, and the parts cost next to the bengkel price.

13
00:00:51,336 --> 00:00:57,292
SAM 3.1 marks the parts on your own photo, not on some generic diagram.

14
00:00:57,292 --> 00:01:00,306
Before step one, there's a short safety checklist.

15
00:01:00,306 --> 00:01:03,296
The steps stay locked until it's done.

16
00:01:03,296 --> 00:01:08,926
Point the camera, and SAM 3.1 outlines the part to touch, about once a second.

17
00:01:08,926 --> 00:01:13,668
Here it's Chromium's test camera playing a sample photo.

18
00:01:13,668 --> 00:01:19,212
After each step, you send a photo, and Muse Spark compares it with what it should look like.

19
00:01:19,212 --> 00:01:22,624
This one's too dark, so it asks for a retake.

20
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:27,380
A clear photo of the plug cap back on passes, and it moves on.

21
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:28,229
Hands dirty?

22
00:01:28,229 --> 00:01:29,574
Turn on hands-free.

23
00:01:29,574 --> 00:01:34,944
It reads each step out loud and listens for simple voice commands.

24
00:01:34,944 --> 00:01:35,822
Still broken?

25
00:01:35,822 --> 00:01:40,147
Tell it what happened, and it moves on to the next likely cause.

26
00:01:40,147 --> 00:01:42,604
Plan, act, check, re-plan.

27
00:01:42,604 --> 00:01:50,720
When a photo can't show a step, like the washer inside a tap, Muse Image draws a diagram, and Muse Spark checks it.

28
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:57,780
Every decision stays on screen: what it saw, why it asked, each photo check, and which model did it.

29
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:02,452
When it's a job for a pro, one tap hands it over: a WhatsApp summary,

30
00:02:02,452 --> 00:02:06,808
the nearest bengkel, and a PDF brief for the mechanic.

31
00:02:06,808 --> 00:02:08,844
And it knows when to say no.

32
00:02:08,844 --> 00:02:17,252
A rice cooker that won't heat means opening 220 volt parts, so it stops and sends you to a service centre.

33
00:02:17,252 --> 00:02:20,545
“Kran pawonku netes terus, piye iki?”

34
00:02:20,545 --> 00:02:23,234
It works in WhatsApp too, in Javanese.

35
00:02:23,234 --> 00:02:30,733
Send a photo, and the same agent replies with the marked photo, the diagnosis, and a button for each step.

36
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:33,768
A gas leak still gets a red stop.

37
00:02:33,768 --> 00:02:37,905
Under the hood: Voice Transcribe, Muse Spark to see,

38
00:02:37,905 --> 00:02:44,509
reason and check, SAM 3.1 for masks and live tracking, and Muse Image for diagrams.

39
00:02:44,509 --> 00:02:47,596
The safety rules live in code.

40
00:02:47,596 --> 00:02:48,627
Tukang Copilot.

41
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:53,096
Every phone becomes a mechanic's apprentice.
